---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { YEAR, LAST_UPDATED, AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, AUTHOR_ROLE } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { personSchema, organizationSchema, breadcrumbSchema, profilePageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Notary fees calculator France: who publishes it and how`} description={`Who publishes this French notary fees calculator, where its rates come from, how it is checked and funded. An independent publisher, unrelated to notaries.`} lang={lang} jsonLd={[personSchema(lang), organizationSchema(lang), profilePageSchema({ path: route('about', lang), lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'About', path: route('about', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">About</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <p><strong>{AUTHOR_NAME}</strong> · {AUTHOR_ROLE[lang]}</p>
    <p>This site is published by Radif Partners, an independent publisher of personal finance calculators and practical guides for several countries. We are not notaries, mortgage brokers or estate agents, and we do not sell your details to professionals: the calculator asks for no personal data and runs in your browser.</p>
    <h2>Why this site</h2>
    <p>Most notary fee simulators apply an average percentage, or a single transfer tax rate for the whole of France. Since départements may raise their rate to 5%, that shortcut is wrong by hundreds to thousands of euros depending on the location. We therefore built the calculation from the official DGFiP table, département by département, with the regulated emolument scale, overseas included, the first-time buyer rule and the reduction voted by Savoie. The English version is written for people who live, work or buy property in France without being familiar with French terms.</p>
    <h2>Our method</h2>
    <p>Every parameter comes from an official source we have read, cited on the page that uses it: impots.gouv.fr for départemental rates, service-public.fr for the scales, Notaires de France for elements of the tariff. Parameters live in a data file, never in the text: every figure shown is recalculated from that file. Automated tests replay the official examples at every change. The <a href={route('method', lang)}>methodology</a> sets out the formula and its limits.</p>
    <h2>Funding</h2>
    <p>The site is free. It may display discreet advertising, never above the calculator; no user data is sold, and no partnership determines the content.</p>
    <h2>Reporting an error</h2>
    <p>A départemental rate that changed, a revised scale, a calculation error? Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. The correction procedure is described in the <a href={route('editorial', lang)}>editorial policy</a>. See also the <a href={route('legal', lang)}>legal notice</a> and the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-navy-500">{YEAR} parameters, updated {displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, 'en-GB')}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
